      "reasoning": "The learner correctly identified D(8; 5). Now they need to find C. In a rhombus, all sides are equal. We know AD = 5. Therefore, CD must also be 5. Since CD is vertical (perpendicular to x-axis), the distance between D(8;5) and C(8; y) is 5. So |5 - y| = 5. This means y = 0 or y = 10. Looking at the position of B(-1; -4), C(8; 0) is the logical vertex for the rhombus ADCB. I will guide them to use the side length property of a rhombus to find the y-coordinate of C. [TOOL CHECK: calculator(expression=\"5 - 5\") -> 0].",
